{"from": "text:nehemiah-3-1", "type": "related_to", "to": "place:sheep-gate", "note": "Biblical cross-reference, not evidence: Nehemiah 3:1 names the sheep gate that Eliashib the high priest and the priests built and sanctified after the exile."}
{"from": "text:nehemiah-3-1", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:jn-05-02-bethesda-pool", "note": "Biblical cross-reference: the Sheep Gate of Nehemiah 3:1 is the gate John 5:2 locates the pool by; Nehemiah does not mention the pool."}
{"from": "claim:jn-05-01-feast-jerusalem", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:jn-02-13-passover-pilgrimage", "note": "Difference: the feast of 5:1 is unnamed, while John 2:13 names a Passover; commentators dispute whether 5:1 is another Passover, so no calendar point is fixed."}
{"from": "claim:jn-05-01-feast-jerusalem", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-02-41-annual-passover", "note": "Same custom, unnamed feast: Luke 2:41 records the annual festival pilgrimage of Jesus's family; John 5:1 has Jesus going up for a feast the Gospel does not name."}
{"from": "claim:jn-05-10-carrying-mat-sabbath", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-12-10-sabbath-healing-debate", "note": "Difference: both controversies turn on what is lawful on the Sabbath, but Matthew 12:10 is about healing on the Sabbath, while John 5:10 objects to carrying a mat; different incidents."}
{"from": "claim:jn-05-10-carrying-mat-sabbath", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-14-02-04-healed-sabbath", "note": "Difference: Luke 14 records a Sabbath healing questioned by the watchers; John 5:9-10 objects to the healed man's carrying his mat on the Sabbath; different incidents."}
{"from": "claim:jn-05-33-john-testified", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:jn-01-19-priests-levites-sent", "note": "Same ministry recalled: John 1:19 narrates priests and Levites sent from Jerusalem to John the Baptist; 5:33 recalls that delegation ('you have sent to John')."}
{"from": "passage:jn-05-33", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-11-07", "note": "Same tradition of Jesus affirming John the Baptist's witness: Matthew 11:7-9 speaks to the crowds about John; John 5:33-35 tells the Jerusalem Jews they sent to John, 'a burning and shining lamp'."}
{"from": "passage:jn-05-33", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:lk-07-24", "note": "Same tradition of Jesus affirming John the Baptist's witness: Luke 7:24-26 addresses John's messengers and the crowds; John 5:33-35 is addressed to the Jerusalem Jews - same substance, different audience."}
